{
  "route_comment": [
    "",
    "Optional CA reader routing (nowa #2). Empty by default - Tvheadend",
    "queries every ENABLED CA client for every scrambled service, exactly",
    "like before this file existed.",
    "",
    "Add entries to the \"route\" list below to restrict which configured",
    "CA clients (by their Title/Name in Configuration -> Conditional",
    "Access) are even TRIED for services carrying a given CAID. Useful",
    "when several card-sharing servers only cover some CAIDs, or when a",
    "server limits you to one concurrent stream and querying it for CAIDs",
    "it can't decode anyway just causes collisions (\"Already has a key",
    "for service\" / NOK).",
    "",
    "caid   - CAID (hexadecimal)",
    "mask   - CAID mask (hexadecimal - use FFFF for a single CAID)",
    "allow  - comma-separated list of CA client names. If set, ONLY these",
    "         clients are started for services carrying this CAID.",
    "deny   - comma-separated list of CA client names to exclude. Only",
    "         used when \"allow\" is not set on the same rule.",
    "",
    "This file is hot-reloaded (checked every ~15s), same as",
    "\"descrambler\" - no restart needed, just re-tune affected channels",
    "for the new rule to take effect.",
    "",
    "Example (commented out):",
    "  { \"caid\": \"1884\", \"mask\": \"FFFF\", \"allow\": \"testowy,s2.skyhd1\" }",
    "  { \"caid\": \"1861\", \"mask\": \"FFFF\", \"deny\": \"s1.skyhd1\" }"
  ],
  "route": [
  ]
}
